{"book": "gate-da", "num": 13, "label": "13", "slug": "13-matrices-matrix-factorizations", "title": "Matrix Factorizations", "tag": "Matrices & Linear Algebra", "summary": "LU Decomposition factorizes a square matrix $A$ as", "wordCount": 153, "readingTimeMin": 1, "intro": [], "sections": [{"id": "13.1", "title": "LU Decomposition", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>LU Decomposition</b> factorizes a square matrix $A$ as"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = LU,"}, {"t": "p", "x": "where $L$ is a lower triangular matrix with unit diagonal entries and $U$ is an upper triangular matrix."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Advantages:</b>\n1. Efficiently solves $Ax=b$ for multiple $b$ without repeating elimination.\n2. Simplifies determinant computation: $\\det(A) = \\det(L)\\det(U) = \\prod_i u_{ii}$.\n3. Simplifies computation of $A^{-1}$ by solving $LUx = e_i$ for each column of the identity."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "97", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Find the LU decomposition of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Let"}, {"t": "math", "x": "L = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ l_{21} & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \nU = \\begin{bmatrix} u_{11} & u_{12} \\\\ 0 & u_{22} \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Matching $LU = A$:"}, {"t": "p", "x": "First row: $u_{11} = 2$, $u_{12} = 3$.\nSecond row: $l_{21} u_{11} = 4 \\implies l_{21} = 2$,\n$l_{21} u_{12} + u_{22} = 7 \\implies 2 \\cdot 3 + u_{22} = 7 \\implies u_{22} = 1$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "Thus,"}, {"t": "math", "x": "L = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad \nU = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "98", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Solve"}, {"t": "math", "x": "\\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\end{bmatrix} \n\\begin{bmatrix} x \\\\ y \\\\ z \\end{bmatrix} = \n\\begin{bmatrix} 3 \\\\ 24 \\\\ 15 \\end{bmatrix}"}, {"t": "p", "x": "using LU decomposition."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Factor $A = LU$, then solve $Ly = b$ (forward substitution):"}, {"t": "math", "x": "y_1 = 3, \\quad y_2 = 24 - 2\\cdot3 = 18, \\quad y_3 = 15 - (-1\\cdot3 + 2\\cdot18) = -21"}, {"t": "p", "x": "Next, solve $Ux = y$ (backward substitution):"}, {"t": "math", "x": "x = 2, \\quad y = 1, \\quad z = 0"}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "99", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "For"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 3 \\end{bmatrix},"}, {"t": "p", "x": "find LU decomposition."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Let $L = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ l_{21} & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, $U = \\begin{bmatrix} u_{11} & u_{12} \\\\ 0 & u_{22} \\end{bmatrix}$."}, {"t": "p", "x": "From $LU = A$: $u_{11}=4$, $u_{12}=3$, $l_{21} u_{11}=6 \\implies l_{21}=1.5$, $l_{21} u_{12}+u_{22}=3 \\implies u_{22}=-1.5$."}, {"t": "math", "x": "L = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 1.5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\nU = \\begin{bmatrix} 4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1.5\\end{bmatrix}."}]}, {"t": "box", "kind": "example", "name": "Example", "num": "100", "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "Determine LU decomposition of"}, {"t": "math", "x": "A = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 5 \\end{bmatrix}."}, {"t": "p", "x": "<b>Solution:</b> Apply elimination:"}, {"t": "math", "x": "L = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1.5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1.5 & 0 & 1 \\end{bmatrix}, \\quad\nU = \\begin{bmatrix} 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4.5 & 7.5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 \\end{bmatrix}."}]}]}, {"id": "13.2", "title": "Applications of LU Factorization", "blocks": [{"t": "box", "kind": "theorem", "name": "Concept", "num": null, "title": null, "blocks": [{"t": "p", "x": "<b>Applications of LU Factorization:</b>\n\n1. <b>Solving linear systems efficiently:</b> Avoid repeated elimination for multiple RHS vectors.\n\n2. <b>Determinant computation:</b> $\\det(A) = \\prod u_{ii}$.\n\n3. <b>Matrix inversion:</b> Solve $LUx = e_i$ for each column of identity.\n\n4. <b>Numerical stability:</b> LU with pivoting improves solution accuracy.\n\n5. <b>Engineering and scientific computations:</b> Widely used in simulations and optimization problems."}]}]}], "sectionCount": 2}